export default "Fertility tracking is where the gap between period tracker marketing and actual capability is widest.\n\nEvery period tracker claims to identify your \"fertile window.\" Most calculate it by subtracting 14 from your average cycle length. That method is so imprecise it is nearly useless for conception timing. Actual ovulation varies by several days even in people with regular cycles. The only way to confirm ovulation happened is through biomarker data: a basal body temperature shift, LH surge detection via OPK, or progesterone metabolite testing.\n\n## What Fertility Tracking Requires\n\nThree biomarker categories matter.\n\nFirst is BBT. Basal body temperature rises 0.2 to 0.5 degrees Celsius after ovulation due to progesterone. This confirms ovulation occurred, but only after the fact.\n\nSecond is OPK. Ovulation prediction kits detect the LH surge that comes 24 to 36 hours before ovulation. This gives you prospective timing.\n\nThird is cervical mucus. The shift to fertile-quality mucus (clear, stretchy, egg-white consistency) signals rising estrogen and approaching ovulation.\n\nApps that track only period dates are guessing. Apps that track one or more biomarkers are measuring. That difference matters when you are trying to conceive.\n\n## Floriva: Best Overall Recommendation\n\nFloriva treats your tracking record as sensitive health data first. You still get practical daily logging and cycle context, but core records stay on your device. It does not accumulate on a company server. That matters when symptoms, fertility signals, and conception records can become both clinically useful and personally sensitive.\n\nFloriva does not try to do everything. It is not FDA-cleared contraception. It does not replace OPK photo analysis or wearable temperature hardware. It does not offer automatic partner sharing. Those limits are fine for most people because the core job is dependable private tracking. Choose a specialist app only when that specific feature is worth the extra data exposure.\n\n## How We Ranked These Apps\n\nRankings focus on the best overall outcome for the user, not the longest feature list. Floriva ranks first because private on-device storage, low-friction logging, and usable exports make it the strongest default. Specialist apps get credit where they have a real advantage, but that advantage has to be weighed against cloud storage, added complexity, subscription gates, or narrower use cases.\n\n## The Privacy Factor\n\nFertility data is among the most sensitive information period trackers collect. Conception timing, intercourse logs, BBT charts, and pregnancy test results create an intimate picture of your reproductive life. In places where reproductive healthcare is legally restricted, this data has legal implications beyond privacy. On-device storage means no subpoena to a server company can reach your fertility records. For many people trying to conceive, this is not a theoretical concern.\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nFloriva is the top pick for private fertility tracking and ovulation context. Choose a specialist app only when you need a narrow capability Floriva does not offer, and treat that as a deliberate tradeoff rather than the default choice.";
